// `todo()` in a `comptime` block is a compile error like any other failure to
// compute it (ctrl.comptime/CT69). It used to be the exception — the const ran
// at run time instead — but a value that's sometimes computed while compiling
// and sometimes not is one nobody can reason about (#1552).
const D: i64 = comptime { todo("write the table") }

func main() { println(D.display()) }
